      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-17T14:08:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know we talked about this, but I don\u0027t love that once we have #version controlling access to these features, we\u0027re going to need a back-door here. This may just make me think harder about some kind of first-class hack for specializations.\n\nAlternatively (in this case): we could just eliminate the specialization for EdgeCount? That would reduce shader combinations, too...\n\nI think all we need to do is fill all the unused edges with [0,0,1]? It makes polygons with few sides slower, but probably isn\u0027t that bad - we already have special cases for rectangles, and how many people are clipping against triangles?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 64,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 64,
        "endChar": 99
      },
      "revId": "3b108257c05680dd1c4fb704ff6f294d597bd3f3",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8b34c4f8_d86e5e5f",
        "filename": "src/gpu/ganesh/effects/GrConvexPolyEffect.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 64,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-17T14:24:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Eliminating the EdgeCount specialization makes this shader _actually_ not-ES2-compliant (for loop can\u0027t be unrolled), so that\u0027s a bit of a non-starter.\n\nI think if we\u0027re going to pessimize the algorithm to always do 8 loops, we\u0027re probably better off just leaving it as a non-runtime effect. It\u0027s hard for me to justify making a change if it\u0027s going to lead to actual worse drawing performance. \n\nHaving run into this twice in a row now I do agree that it\u0027s very limiting that specializations are treated differently in the initial parse vs in the final output. I think it\u0027d be worth adding a little extra syntactic sugar to allow specializations to be treated as constant values.\n\nShould I abandon this for now? It\u0027s NBD, I didn\u0027t spend long on it.",
      "parentUuid": "781fad1a_5324e15d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 64,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 64,
        "endChar": 99
      },
      "revId": "3b108257c05680dd1c4fb704ff6f294d597bd3f3",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
